# Astro and Supabase boundaries

- Keep API routes thin; place reusable persistence in `src/lib/services/` and
  deterministic decisions in pure functions under `src/lib/`.
- Validate request bodies with the shared Zod contracts before persistence and
  preserve the documented 400/401/404/409/500 JSON behavior.
- Use the public Supabase key only in browser code. Never add a `service_role`
  key to application runtime, client code, or CI.
- RLS is mandatory for user-owned data. A schema or policy change needs a
  migration contract assertion and hosted RLS verification before release.
- Keep the existing Polish UI language and accessible semantic HTML. Do not
  add LLM calls, payments, teams, imports, notifications, gamification, or
  advanced SRS without expanding the approved MVP contract.
